  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 858 AM MST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nTODAY:\n\nA shortwave trough is expected to move through the area today. This \nwill bring some high clouds to the sky, with a chance for isolated \nshowers over the higher terrain. Accumulations, if any, will be on \nthe lighter side. Overnight cloud cover will moderate overnight lows \nand preclude the notion of any valley fog development. Beyond Friday \nnight, the shortwave moves off to our east, with an expansive ridge \nof high pressure moving in from the west. \n\nDRY AND MILD WEEKEND:\n\nAs high pressure materializes over the region, dry and milder \nweather will be on tap for the foreseeable future. This will give us \na much needed break from the recent abundant precipitation. Looking \nahead towards next week, some systems will be rotating near the \nPacNW, but as those traverse eastward, storm tracks remain north, \nkeeping us in a drier period even longer. Daytime highs under this \nridge will be seasonable, if not above normal at times.",
